cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the PocketGull Font Superfamily in clinical software, medical informatics, vision science research, or assistive reading systems, please cite it as below."
title: "PocketGull Font Superfamily: Optotypically Calibrated Clinical, Mathematical, Astronomical & Telemetry Vector Letterforms"
abstract: "PocketGull is an open-source clinical sans-serif, display, mathematical, and telemetry monospace font superfamily bridging tactile humanist warmth with zero-error clinical precision. Engineered on a 1000 UPM grid conforming to ISO/IEC 14496-22 and Google Fonts specifications with LogMAR 0.0 Snellen optotypic geometry, PocketGull incorporates 256 Unicode Braille patterns (U+2800..U+28FF), ISMP/FDA numeral disambiguation (slashed zero, curved lowercase l, serifed capital I, slashed Z), Louise Sloan 5:1 proportional legibility, Scotopic 650nm dark-sky red mode for astronomical observatories, 80-column FITS header compliance, robust 68 UPM math stem weights with OpenType MATH tables (LaTeX CTAN / Typst universe), gapless ICU telemetry box drawing (U+2500..U+257F) with sub-cell plethysmograph/ECG waveforms, and native multi-script support for Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics, Chinuk Pipa, Cherokee Syllabary, Neo-Tifinagh, Ethiopic Ge'ez, Adlam, Vai, and Pan-Tribal North American Indigenous orthographies under the CARE Principles for Indigenous Data Sovereignty."
